# netsurf: a sheet-change mark carries the sheet's identity (doc 23 piece A, patch 318)
# Generated 2026-10-25
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 317)
#
# Doc 23 piece A ("sheet identity on the mark"), the piece patch 316's
# census deferred. A sheet change reaches the reconvert as a nodeless
# mark; nothing on it says which stylesheet changed, so no later stage
# could answer the batch from that sheet. Behaviour is unchanged here:
# identified batches still take the full reconvert, and the FULLCAUSE /
# BATCHCAUSE / SHEETCAUSE formats the gate matches stay as they are.
#
#  - html.h: struct html_stylesheet gains mod_count, the per-entry
#    modification counter (bumped at the top of
#    html_css_process_modified_style, before the new sheet can finish
#    and mark), and mark_pending (the entry held for patch 266's
#    deferred refresh).
#  - css.c: both sheet-mark sites go through html_css_mark_sheets(c, i).
#    The settle window's set is the finishing entry, the entry held for
#    the deferred refresh, and every entry still in flight (queued for
#    re-processing, or its sheet still loading) -- that one will mark
#    into the same window. A singleton set emits
#    macos9_js_mark_dom_dirty_sheet(c, index, counter); anything else
#    emits the nodeless mark as before. html_css_sheet_mark_current()
#    answers whether an entry is still at the counter its mark carried.
#    (Doc 23's "entries processed since the last mark" is read as
#    "in flight": entries the initial parse processed bump the counter
#    without ever marking, and counting them made every first
#    post-layout mark multi.)
#  - macos9_reconvert.c/.h: macos9_js_mark_dom_dirty_sheet records the
#    nodeless mark exactly as macos9_js_mark_dom_dirty does, with the
#    identity alongside. The slot folds every nodeless mark's identity
#    (also into a slot already coarse): none / one entry (index + the
#    FIRST mark's counter) / more than one, plus a flag for a nodeless
#    mark without identity. At the commit of a nonode batch the flush
#    logs "LIFE SHEETID single|stale idx= ctr=" (one entry; stale =
#    re-processed before the flush, so an answer from that mark would
#    use the wrong sheet pair), "LIFE SHEETID multi" or
#    "LIFE SHEETID none", and the navigation reset prints
#    "LIFE SHEETIDCENSUS single= stale= multi= none=".
#
# Proof (focused, sim, JS-sheet-census, now 3 steps): the one-<style>
# edit logs SHEETID single idx=5 (agreeing with patch 316's sheets=1),
# the two-<style> task logs SHEETID multi (sheets=2), and the new step
# 3 -- one <style> edited twice 150 ms apart, the second edit landing
# after the first's DONE but before its batch flushed -- logs SHEETID
# stale, with the final style the second edit's (SHEETCENSUS 3/3). A
# 40 ms gap coalesces the two edits into one process instead (one
# DONE, counter current), as the doc's design expects.
#
# Not done (doc 23 pieces B/C, recorded): no reach analysis, no local
# answer from an identified batch; the text-node mark each <style> edit
# also produces (patch 316's finding) is untouched.
#
# Simulator only; the vita cross-build was not run for this patch.
